# ==============================================================================
# Corpora and everything derived from them. All rebuildable, none belongs in git.
# This is ~3.6 GB: dataset_v5 alone is 904 MB and speech_corpus is 1.2 GB.
# ==============================================================================
*.npz
*.npy
dataset/
dataset_*/
noise_bank/
noise_bank_v2/
speech_corpus/
corpus_cache/
cache/
logs/
.kaggle-outputs/
*.wav

# ==============================================================================
# Credentials. The notebook hardcodes a live Kaggle API key, and the session export
# below contains the conversation where it was pasted. Tracking either one would put a
# working credential in the history, where deleting the file later does NOT remove it.
#
# To track the notebook, move the key to an environment variable first:
#     KAGGLE_API_KEY = os.environ["KAGGLE_API_KEY"]
# then remove these two lines from this file.
# ==============================================================================
kaggle_self_contained.ipynb
session-ses_*.md
kaggle.json

# ==============================================================================
# Model weights: the experiments are reproducible from the code, so only the two
# checkpoints the documentation actually references are tracked.
# ==============================================================================
*.flax
!best_v3_50k.flax
!best_50k_kws_model.flax

# ==============================================================================
# Python
# ==============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ==============================================================================
# OS / editor
# ==============================================================================
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
